cff-version: 1.2.0
title: bev-calibration-lab
message: >-
  If you use this software or its published evidence, please cite it using the
  metadata below, and cite nuScenes as listed under references.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kuo
    given-names: Tun-Yu
    alias: kuotunyu
repository-code: https://github.com/kuotunyu/bev-calibration-lab
url: https://kuotunyu.github.io/bev-calibration-lab/
abstract: >-
  A controlled study of LiDAR-camera extrinsic calibration faults on nuScenes.
  Single-axis rotation and translation faults are injected into the CAM_FRONT
  extrinsic of a locked evaluation cohort, and identity, a single-frame
  edge-alignment optimizer and three seeds of a ConvNeXtV2-Tiny corrector are
  compared with paired scene-bootstrap intervals. The mean of the three learned
  seeds beats the classical optimizer on geodesic rotation error, translation-norm
  error, pixel error and recovery in every condition of the fault grid but keeps a
  residual error floor, so it improves on leaving the calibration alone only for
  larger faults. Every published number is bound to
  the committed evidence by a machine-checked claims registry.
keywords:
  - autonomous-driving
  - sensor-fusion
  - lidar-camera-calibration
  - extrinsic-calibration
  - nuscenes
  - reproducibility
